<<PlayBackgroundMusic Exciting_1>> 
<<SetBGSprite hutInterior>>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Captain… you sleeping?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Tired">>
Raju: Bhai? Is it school already?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Not yet. It's good news o'clock.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Did we… are we…?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Maa and Baba said yes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Yes… like yes yes?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Like "open window, let the wind in" yes - three months of routine, respect, and no shortcuts.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: They really said it?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Baba said "No money wasted, marks steady, manners steady" and Maa touched the bat and my forehead - that's permission with a blessing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: What if I mess up?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Then we learn, fix, and try again. We don't let poverty steal our manners—or our second chances.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: What do we do first?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: First, we say thank you through small actions - keep the bat face-up when it rests and our promises upright all day.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Ok.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Our promise stack - up with the first bell, water bottle filled, chores done, school on time, then half an hour of study with me. If the page is messy, the ground is off-limits next morning.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Deal. Will you be there every time?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Every dawn I'm your shadow. You won't carry cost; you'll carry care.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Baba will still have pain in his knees - maybe I can heat the towel before we go?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: That's the spirit - dreamers who help at home dream longer, so add warm towel for Baba and tea for Maa to the routine.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Bhai… today the ground will feel different?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Today the ground will know your name was spoken at home with blessing. That changes how dust rises under your feet.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I can't Wait.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Remember our five coins?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Eyes, feet, hands, timing, temper.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Keep them in your pocket, and when noise gets loud, touch each one in your mind and breathe to keep your promise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: What should I call these three months?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Confident">>
Ramu: A season, not a test - tests end with marks, but seasons end with learning.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: If I shine…?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: We will take it as it comes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Face up and chin up.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Loving">>
Ramu: And heart steady - touch the floor, touch your heart, then tie your laces before the bell rings.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Thank you Maa, Baba, bat, and Bhai.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: From today, you practice like you're choosing yourself. Let's go open that window.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
